.TH LEVEE 1 "Riplix" "Ripple"
.SH NAME
levee \- edit text with vi commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
levee [file]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Levee is an alternative vi-style editor. Start in command mode: h, j, k, l move the
cursor; i inserts text; Escape returns to command mode; x deletes a
character; dd deletes a line; u undoes; / searches.
.PP
:w writes the buffer, :w filename sets a new filename, :q quits an unchanged
buffer, :wq saves and quits, and :q! quits while discarding changes.
Ctrl-C cancels raw input. The editor restores the terminal on exit.
.PP
The buffer holds at most 29999 native characters. Terminal dimensions are
validated; this is a small vi implementation rather than full Vim.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
levee notes
.fi
